{"parentUuid":"b71546f2-e05a-4a01-81e7-52130ec22079","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyoEun2eJwBcCdTNdkYT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The disk is full again: 122Mi free. Turning on iced's `advanced` feature rebuilt iced, which used about 4Gi. The last build and test run stopped for lack of space, so this round is **not committed**.\n\n**Done, uncommitted:**\n- **Hover lift on everything clickable.** `crates/bastion-desktop/src/lift.rs` adds a `Lift` wrapper widget that draws its content 4% larger while the pointer is over it. `lift::button` keeps the same builder methods as iced's button.\n  - All 69 `button(` calls across 21 desktop files now use it. The theme's styles are unchanged.\n  - That needed iced's `advanced` feature, now enabled in `crates/bastion-desktop/Cargo.toml`.\n  - Clippy `-D warnings` passed on the desktop crate after the swap. I haven't seen it running in the app yet.\n- **Journey wording.** A workflow is a trail, and a job is a journey along it. The job's chart is titled \"THE JOURNEY\", with the note \"this job, along its workflow's trail\". The Map now says workflows are \"trails every job journeys along\". PLAN.md records both.\n- **Already pushed: 068e3b6,** the way home, field notes and the atlas (D59). That ran with full CI: 330 tests passed.\n\n**Still to verify:** clippy and tests after the wording edits, and a live look at the lift. A full rebuild with the new feature needs about 5Gi. Free that, and I'll verify, commit, push, and continue: each harbor town on the Map opening its workspace's atlas, then route wear."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":733171,"output_tokens":696,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache