{"parentUuid":"2df6e64e-64f7-43b4-8c45-35a1c44d30fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgypmnG4VbnMfThT269Xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012iYvvKzXZqdWYEWPZhBSHR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='jobs.rs'; s=open(p).read()\nfor a,b in [('const EVERY: &str = \"Every workspace\";','const EVERY: &str = \"Every region\";'),\n('chart::view(\"Jobs started by day, last 30 days\"','chart::view(\"Journeys set out by day, last 30 days\"'),\n('labeled(\"Workspace\", place)','labeled(\"Region\", place)'),\n('unwrap_or(\"home\")','unwrap_or(\"the summit\")')]:\n    assert a in s, a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\nd=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\na=d[d.index(\"| D59 |\"):].split(\"\\n\",1)[0]\nnew=a+\"\\n| D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |\"\nd=d.replace(a,new,1)\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write(d)\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\na=\"### X. Exploration: learning, discovery, feedback\"\np=p.replace(a,a+'''\n\nNext, the atlas moves (revises D59):\n\n- A note about the region goes into the region's repository, as\n  documentation: appended to its atlas file and committed on a branch,\n  as a charter edit is (D58), for a person to merge. Agents can read it\n  there.\n- A note about Bastion stays in Bastion's database. It is not an atlas:\n  it feeds a learning loop on the Guide, where each note offers to\n  become guidance or a check at the waypoint it came from.\n- Open: the atlas file's path in a repository.''',1)\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncargo fmt && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; scripts/check-seams.sh | tail -1; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result\" | awk '{s+=$4; f+=$6} END {print \"passed\",s,\"failed\",f}'; git add DECISIONS.md PLAN.md crates && git status --short | wc -l","description":"Leftovers, D60, plan; CI; stage","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":784903,"output_tokens":1155,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1155,"cache_read_input_tokens":784903,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012iYvvKzXZqdWYEWPZhBSHR":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='jobs.rs'; s=open(p).read()\nfor a,b in [('const EVERY: &str = \"Every workspace\";','const EVERY: &str = \"Every region\";'),\n('chart::view(\"Jobs started by day, last 30 days\"','chart::view(\"Journeys set out by day, last 30 days\"'),\n('labeled(\"Workspace\", place)','labeled(\"Region\", place)'),\n('unwrap_or(\"home\")','unwrap_or(\"the summit\")')]:\n    assert a in s, a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\nd=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\na=d[d.index(\"| D59 |\"):].split(\"\\n\",1)[0]\nnew=a+\"\\n| D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |\"\nd=d.replace(a,new,1)\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write(d)\np=open('PLAN.md').read()\na=\"### X. Exploration: learning, discovery, feedback\"\np=p.replace(a,a+'''\n\nNext, the atlas moves (revises D59):\n\n- A note about the region goes into the region's repository, as\n  documentation: appended to its atlas file and committed on a branch,\n  as a charter edit is (D58), for a person to merge. Agents can read it\n  there.\n- A note about Bastion stays in Bastion's database. It is not an atlas:\n  it feeds a learning loop on the Guide, where each note offers to\n  become guidance or a check at the waypoint it came from.\n- Open: the atlas file's path in a repository.''',1)\nopen('PLAN.md','w').write(p)\nEOF\ncargo fmt && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; scripts/check-seams.sh | tail -1; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result\" | awk '{s+=$4; f+=$6} END {print \"passed\",s,\"failed\",f}'; git add DECISIONS.md PLAN.md crates && git status --short | wc -l","description":"Leftovers, D60, plan; CI; stage","timeout":900000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_012iYvvKzXZqdWYEWPZhBSHR":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"515129f3-5874-42d6-82e1-b3340c462b9b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgypmmqGfs4bqqD7vwjvM","type":"assistant","uu