{"parentUuid":"f7fa4692-8646-4e8e-839c-5ed9037004c5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c38463d1-54bb-47be-a5be-70235405c515","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012iYvvKzXZqdWYEWPZhBSHR","type":"tool_result","content":"seams ok\npassed 330 failed 0\n      15\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5dc04850-bf19-48ff-b403-fbb40caa121c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:30:01.305Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"seams ok\npassed 330 failed 0\n      15","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":86,"oldLines":6,"newStart":86,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D57 | Rules live on three pages, Constraints, Capabilities and Permissions, each with a Global view and a Workflows view that picks the workflows and steps an item applies to. A step lists what applies at it, read-only. The charter shows on a Workspaces page; Bastion still applies it, but it is not edited with Bastion's rules. This replaces D53's \"no Constraints or Capabilities page\". |"," | D58 | Nothing is global. Each rule, agent, skill, hook, reviewer and grant applies only where it is selected: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows. An item with no selection applies nowhere. A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch. Every page shows all servers or one; on All servers a row names its server, and a change goes to that server. This replaces D57's Global view with All workflows, and D53's rule that only record pages span servers. |"," | D59 | A field note is what a job taught, one sentence signed by the person who wrote it, about the workspace (the project) or about Bastion (its workflows and harness). It is an audit entry on the job, so the chain signs it and nothing rewrites it. A workspace's notes are its atlas, where the next request starts. A job that comes home, landed or in the marsh, draws its way back to the atlas. |","+| D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":299,"oldLines":6,"newStart":299,"newLines":17,"lines":[" "," ### X. Exploration: learning, discovery, feedback"," ","+Next, the atlas moves (revises D59):","+","+- A note about the region goes into the region's repository, as","+  documentation: appended to its atlas file and committed on a branch,","+  as a charter edit is (D58), for a person to merge. Agents can read it","+  there.","+- A note about Bastion stays in Bastion's database. It is not an atlas:","+  it feeds a learning loop on the Guide, where each note offers to","+  become guidance or a check at the waypoint it came from.","+- Open: the atlas file's path in a repository.","+"," The app should feel like an expedition, and improve itself from what jobs"," teach."," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/jobs.rs","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" use crate::theme;"," "," const FINISHED: [&str; 3] = [\"landed\", \"failed\", \"stopped\"];","-const EVERY: &str = \"Every workspace\";","+const EVERY: &str = \"Every region\";"," "," /// A job, and the Bastion server it runs on (D30)."," #[derive(Clone, Debug)]"]},{"oldStart":192,"oldLines":7,"newStart":192,"newLines":12,"lines":["             .size(12)","             .color(theme::muted()),","     );","-    let at = sj.job.node.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"home\").replace('_', \" \");","+    let at = sj","+        .job","+        .node","+        .as_deref()","+        .unwrap_or(\"the summit\")","+        .replace('_', \" \");","     let stage = container(text(at).size(12))","         .padding([2, 8])","         .style(theme::chip);"]},{"oldStart":301,"oldLines":7,"newStart":306,"newLines":7,"lines":["     let now = std::time::SystemTime::now()","         .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)","         .map_or(0, |d| d.as_secs());","-    let chart = chart::view(\"Jobs started by day, last 30 days\", started(jobs, now));","+    let chart = chart::view(\"Journeys set out by day, last 30 days\", started(jobs, now));","     column![tiles, chart].spacing(12).into()"," }"," "]},{"oldStart":314,"oldLines":7,"newStart":319,"newLines":7,"lines":["         .on_input(|s| Message::Jobs(Msg::Search(s)))","         .style(theme::field)","         .width(260);","-    row![labeled(\"Workspace\", place), labeled(\"Search\", search)]","+    row![labeled(\"Region\", place), labeled(\"Search\", search)]","         .spacing(12)","         .into()"," }"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/jobs.rs"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"515129f3-5874-42d6-82e1-b3340c462b9b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":13,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"o