{"parentUuid":"c97a7044-8e10-437d-89c9-d7cd10b5fdda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyrGZ5V2XFtt67BXzFeM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012FoKvtHfQWFbCqkdBCj25H","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Find path-triggered context hook","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"In the Rust repo at /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion (crates/bastion-server, crates/bastion-core, workers/), find how an agent's tool calls flow through Bastion's gate, and whether Bastion can add text to what the agent receives after a call. Answer precisely, with file:line references:\n1. Where the gate judges a call (pre-call): the function, what it gets (function name, path/text of a sandbox::fs::read or write call), and what it can return (continue/deny/ask, anything else?).\n2. Is there any post-call hook or place where a call's RESULT passes through Bastion code (so text could be appended to a read's result)? Look for after/post/result handling in gate.rs, engine/, factory, and the workers/ (e.g. bastion-mcp). Also check how iii-sdk triggers/hooks are bound for the gate (\"pre-trigger hook\", binds [\"*\"]).\n3. How the charter is read for a job (charter.rs read(), BRIEF_FILES, .agents/settings.json) and how a brief/turn prompt is built (where AGENTS.md text is put into the agent's brief). Name the function that builds the brief.\n4. Whether a turn's brief is built once per turn or per step, and whether a turn can be told new text mid-turn (e.g. a \"note\" or feedback injected).\nKeep the answer under 400 words. Do not suggest designs, only report what exists."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1297,"cache_read_input_tokens":797068,"output_tokens":1246,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":511},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier