{"parentUuid":"e3b84f5d-94b8-4cbd-b7c5-e07e5d52fda4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyrMKnvWgMw2A2sEcz2E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2156,"cache_read_input_tokens":801430,"output_tokens":1085,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":493},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2156,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1085,"cache_read_input_tokens":801430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2156},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"07b7eeab-510a-4ecb-a50e-045df2d3ad37","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgyrMKFgWEGcyuqNx5xaJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3819bd5-34b1-4db0-9514-90650d64461a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:50:26.081Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"b3819bd5-34b1-4db0-9514-90650d64461a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyrMKnvWgMw2A2sEcz2E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The report settles the mechanism. The gate sees each read and write call's path before the call runs. A call's result reaches Bastion only when the gate **holds** the call and runs it itself: it does this today for calls that ask first, and returns the result with `resolve`. So:\n\n- **How the corpus loads:** when an agent opens a path that matches an unread corpus entry, the gate holds that call and runs it itself. It returns the file with the corpus entry put in front, once per entry per turn.\n- **Cost:** the first matching call in a turn takes one extra trip through Bastion. Later calls don't.\n- **Why not at turn start:** Bastion can't know which paths a turn will open.\n\nI build it in three steps:\n1. **Core:** read a corpus entry's `paths:` globs, and match a path against them. This is pure and testable, with a small glob matcher, since core may only use serde and sha2.\n2. **Server:** read `.agents/corpus/` at the journey's base commit with the charter. The gate injects matching entries through the held-call path.\n3. **App:** signing a region note asks \"rule or fact\", and for a fact, its paths. It then commits to `.agents/rules/` or `.agents/corpus/` on the journey's branch.\n\nI start with step 1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2156,"cache_read_input_tokens":801430,"output_tokens":1085,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":493},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2156,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1085,"cache_read_input_tokens":801430,"cache_creation_inp