X_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":62},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4c77e798-ce7c-4471-a09a-050a1cd7977a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:50:39.829Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"8183922d-5bc7-4f0c-99c3-f36172141cb1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"79eac49e-8545-4619-a366-09be30bd5aaa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015bsHs45uxWbKhajJZ4Kgf1","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cebc0493-7b1f-407b-b196-bc5cff2323fa","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:50:40.008Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":7,"newStart":87,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D58 | Nothing is global. Each rule, agent, skill, hook, reviewer and grant applies only where it is selected: one step, a workflow's steps, some workflows, or all workflows. An item with no selection applies nowhere. A charter's items apply to their workspace's jobs, and the app edits them as a commit on a new branch of the workspace's repository, never on its base branch. Every page shows all servers or one; on All servers a row names its server, and a change goes to that server. This replaces D57's Global view with All workflows, and D53's rule that only record pages span servers. |"," | D59 | A field note is what a job taught, one sentence signed by the person who wrote it, about the workspace (the project) or about Bastion (its workflows and harness). It is an audit entry on the job, so the chain signs it and nothing rewrites it. A workspace's notes are its atlas, where the next request starts. A job that comes home, landed or in the marsh, draws its way back to the atlas. |"," | D60 | The app speaks the expedition: a job is a journey, a workflow a trail, a step a waypoint, a workspace a region, the harness the guide, and the records the logbook (the track, provisions, trials, specimens). A journey is at the outpost, under way, waiting for you, at the summit, or in the marsh. Settings, and the fields that need an industry name (provider, model, API key, token, budget, branch, commit, MCP server), keep their plain names. The code, the API and these decisions keep the precise terms. |","-| D61 | What a journey teaches about its region is a charter change, never a separate atlas, so each repository stays the one source of truth for its project. It is one of two kinds: a rule (codified practice, in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`) or a corpus entry (a fact about structure, a surprise, a scenario for the product, in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, whose `paths:` globs say where it is relevant). An agent is given a corpus entry only when it opens a matching path. Bastion writes charter changes only under `.agents/`, on the journey's own branch, or on a branch of its own for a journey that ends in the marsh. What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database and feeds the learning loop on the Guide. This replaces D59's atlas. |","+| D61 | What a journey teaches about its region is a charter change, never a separate atlas, so each repository stays the one source of truth for its project. It is one of two kinds: a lesson (codified practice: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or a permission in `.agents/settings.json`) or a corpus entry (a fact about structure, a surprise, a scenario for the product, in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`, whose `paths:` globs say where it is relevant). An agent is given a corpus entry only when it opens a matching path. Bastion writes charter changes only under `.agents/`, on the journey's own branch, or on a branch of its own for a journey that ends in the marsh. What a journey teaches about Bastion itself stays in Bastion's database and feeds the learning loop on the Guide. This replaces D59's atlas. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":301,"oldLines":8,"newStart":301,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," Next, notes become charter changes (D61, replacing D59's atlas):"," ","-- Signing a note about the region asks which kind it is. A rule goes to","-  `.agents/rules/<name>.md`; a fact goes to `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`","+- Signing a note about the region asks which kind it is. A lesson is","+  codified: a rule in `.agents/rules/<name>.md`, or a hook or permission","+  in `.agents/settings.json`. A fact goes to `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`","   with the paths it is about. The change is committed on the journey's","   branch, or on a branch of its own when the journey ended in the marsh."," - The corpus is loaded by path: when an agent opens a path a corpus"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"edd43d12-9c3f-46b5-8023-de4cab54de3c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8183922d-5bc7-4f0c-99c3-f36172141cb1","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"cebc0493-7b1f-407b-b196-bc5cff2323fa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_015bsHs45uxWbKhajJZ4Kgf1","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3734d2b3-d636-4a7a-bbae-65ec3a7b0979","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:50:58.211Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"3734d2b3-d636-4a7a-bbae-65ec3a7b0979","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyrNssFcTcfBcoajYVDG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KyPkzyyQ2rh2h4j358ewdn","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/corpus.rs","content":"//! A region's corpus (D61): facts about its structure, its surprises and\n//! its scenarios, each in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`. An entry opens with\n//! the paths it is relevant to, and an agent is given it only when it opens\n//! one of them.\n//!\n//! ```text\n//! ---\n//! paths: src/billing/**, docs/billing.md\n//! ---\n//! Invoices round half to even; the ledger relies on it.\n//! ```\n\n/// Where a repository keeps its corpus.\npub const DIR: &str = \".agents/corpus\";\n\n/// One corpus entry: its name, the path globs it is relevant to, and its\n/// text.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Entry {\n    pub name: String,\n    pub paths: Vec<String>,\n    pub text: String,\n}\n\n/// An entry from its file's name and text. An entry with no `paths:` line\n/// is relevant nowhere, so it is never given.\npub fn parse(name: &str, file: &str) -> Entry {\n    let (head, text) = front_matter(file);\n    let paths = head\n        .lines()\n        .find_map(|l| l.trim().strip_prefix(\"paths:\"))\n        .map(|list| {\n            let globs = list.split(',').map(|g| g.trim().trim_matches(['\"', '\\'']));\n            globs.filter(|g| !g.is_empty()).map(String::from).collect()\n        })\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n    Entry {\n        name: name.trim_end_matches(\".md\").into(),\n        paths,\n        text: text.trim().into(),\n    }\n}\n\n/// The front matter between two `---` lines at the top, and the rest.\nfn front_matter(file: &str) -> (&str, &str) {\n    let Some(rest) = file.trim_start().strip_prefix(\"---\") else {\n        return (\"\", file);\n    };\n    match rest.split_once(\"\\n---\") {\n        Some((head, body)) => (head, body.trim_start_matches('-')),\n        None => (\"\", file),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Whether `path`, relative to the repository, matches `glob`: `*` takes\n/// any characters but `/`, `**` any number of whole parts.\npub fn matches(glob: &str, path: &str) -> bool {\n    let glob: Vec<&str> = glob.trim_start_matches(\"./\").split('/').collect();\n    let path: Vec<&str> = path.trim_start_matches(\"./\").split('/').collect();\n    parts(&glob, &path)\n}\n\nfn parts(glob: &[&str], path: &[&str]) -> bool {\n    match (glob.first(), path.first()) {\n        (None, None) => true,\n        (Some(&\"**\"), _) => {\n            parts(&glob[1..], path) || (!path.is_empty() && parts(glob, &path[1..]))\n        }\n        (Some(g), Some(p)) => part(g, p) && parts(&glob[1..], &path[1..]),\n        _ => false,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Whether one part of a path matches one part of a glob, `*` within it.\nfn part(glob: &str, name: &str) -> bool {\n    match glob.split_once('*') {\n        None => glob == name,\n        Some((head, tail)) => {\n            let Some(rest) = name.strip_prefix(head) else {\n                return false;\n            };\n            (0..=rest.len()).any(|i| rest.is_char_boundary(i) && part(tail, &rest[i..]))\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A path a call opened, relative to the repository: the sandbox mounts\n/// it at `/work/repo`.\npub fn in_repo(path: &str) -> &str {\n    path.strip_prefix(\"/work/repo/\").unwrap_or(path)\n}\n\n/// The entries relevant to `path` that `given` does not hold yet.\npub fn relevant<'a>(entries: &'a [Entry], path: &str, given: &[String]) -> Vec<&'a Entry> {\n    let path = in_repo(path);\n    entries\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|e| !given.contains(&e.name))\n        .filter(|e| e.paths.iter().any(|g| matches(g, path)))\n        .collect()\n}\n\n/// The entries as an agent is given them, ahead of what its call returned.\npub fn told(entries: &[&Entry]) -> String {\n    let each = entries.iter().map(|e| {\n        format!(\n            \"<corpus name=\\\"{}\\\">\\n{}\\n</corpus>\",\n            e.name, e.text\n        )\n    });\n    each.collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\"\\n\")\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn globs_match_whole_parts_and_stars_within_one() {\n        assert!(matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billing/invoice.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billing/tax/vat.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/**/mod.rs\", \"src/a/b/mod.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/*.rs\", \"src/main.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"docs/billing.md\", \"./docs/billing.md\"));\n        assert!(!matches(\"src/*.rs\", \"src/a/main.rs\"), \"* stays in one part\");\n        assert!(!matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billingx/a.rs\"));\n        assert!(!matches(\"docs/billing.md\", \"docs/billing.mdx\"));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn an_entry_reads_its_paths_and_is_given_once_where_it_is_relevant() {\n        let file = \"---\\npaths: src/billing/**, \\\"docs/billing.md\\\"\\n---\\nInvoices round half to even.\\n\";\n        let e = parse(\"rounding.md\", file);\n        assert_eq!(e.name, \"rounding\");\n        assert_eq!(e.paths, [\"src/billing/**\", \"docs/billing.md\"]);\n        assert_eq!(e.text, \"Invoices round half to even.\");\n        let all = [e];\n        let hit = relevant(&all, \"/work/repo/src/billing/a.rs\", &[]);\n        assert_eq!(hit.len(), 1);\n        assert!(relevant(&all, \"/work/repo/src/main.rs\", &[]).is_empty());\n        assert!(relevant(&all, \"src/billing/a.rs\", &[\"rounding\".into()]).is_empty());\n        assert!(told(&hit).contains(\"<corpus name=\\\"rounding\\\">\"));\n        assert!(parse(\"loose.md\", \"No front matter.\").paths.is_empty());\n    }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":805825,"output_tokens":2326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2326,"cache_read_input_tokens":805825,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":845},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KyPkzyyQ2rh2h4j358ewdn":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src/corpus.rs","content":"//! A region's corpus (D61): facts about its structure, its surprises and\n//! its scenarios, each in `.agents/corpus/<name>.md`. An entry opens with\n//! the paths it is relevant to, and an agent is given it only when it opens\n//! one of them.\n//!\n//! ```text\n//! ---\n//! paths: src/billing/**, docs/billing.md\n//! ---\n//! Invoices round half to even; the ledger relies on it.\n//! ```\n\n/// Where a repository keeps its corpus.\npub const DIR: &str = \".agents/corpus\";\n\n/// One corpus entry: its name, the path globs it is relevant to, and its\n/// text.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct Entry {\n    pub name: String,\n    pub paths: Vec<String>,\n    pub text: String,\n}\n\n/// An entry from its file's name and text. An entry with no `paths:` line\n/// is relevant nowhere, so it is never given.\npub fn parse(name: &str, file: &str) -> Entry {\n    let (head, text) = front_matter(file);\n    let paths = head\n        .lines()\n        .find_map(|l| l.trim().strip_prefix(\"paths:\"))\n        .map(|list| {\n            let globs = list.split(',').map(|g| g.trim().trim_matches(['\"', '\\'']));\n            globs.filter(|g| !g.is_empty()).map(String::from).collect()\n        })\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n    Entry {\n        name: name.trim_end_matches(\".md\").into(),\n        paths,\n        text: text.trim().into(),\n    }\n}\n\n/// The front matter between two `---` lines at the top, and the rest.\nfn front_matter(file: &str) -> (&str, &str) {\n    let Some(rest) = file.trim_start().strip_prefix(\"---\") else {\n        return (\"\", file);\n    };\n    match rest.split_once(\"\\n---\") {\n        Some((head, body)) => (head, body.trim_start_matches('-')),\n        None => (\"\", file),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Whether `path`, relative to the repository, matches `glob`: `*` takes\n/// any characters but `/`, `**` any number of whole parts.\npub fn matches(glob: &str, path: &str) -> bool {\n    let glob: Vec<&str> = glob.trim_start_matches(\"./\").split('/').collect();\n    let path: Vec<&str> = path.trim_start_matches(\"./\").split('/').collect();\n    parts(&glob, &path)\n}\n\nfn parts(glob: &[&str], path: &[&str]) -> bool {\n    match (glob.first(), path.first()) {\n        (None, None) => true,\n        (Some(&\"**\"), _) => {\n            parts(&glob[1..], path) || (!path.is_empty() && parts(glob, &path[1..]))\n        }\n        (Some(g), Some(p)) => part(g, p) && parts(&glob[1..], &path[1..]),\n        _ => false,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Whether one part of a path matches one part of a glob, `*` within it.\nfn part(glob: &str, name: &str) -> bool {\n    match glob.split_once('*') {\n        None => glob == name,\n        Some((head, tail)) => {\n            let Some(rest) = name.strip_prefix(head) else {\n                return false;\n            };\n            (0..=rest.len()).any(|i| rest.is_char_boundary(i) && part(tail, &rest[i..]))\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A path a call opened, relative to the repository: the sandbox mounts\n/// it at `/work/repo`.\npub fn in_repo(path: &str) -> &str {\n    path.strip_prefix(\"/work/repo/\").unwrap_or(path)\n}\n\n/// The entries relevant to `path` that `given` does not hold yet.\npub fn relevant<'a>(entries: &'a [Entry], path: &str, given: &[String]) -> Vec<&'a Entry> {\n    let path = in_repo(path);\n    entries\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|e| !given.contains(&e.name))\n        .filter(|e| e.paths.iter().any(|g| matches(g, path)))\n        .collect()\n}\n\n/// The entries as an agent is given them, ahead of what its call returned.\npub fn told(entries: &[&Entry]) -> String {\n    let each = entries.iter().map(|e| {\n        format!(\n            \"<corpus name=\\\"{}\\\">\\n{}\\n</corpus>\",\n            e.name, e.text\n        )\n    });\n    each.collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\"\\n\")\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn globs_match_whole_parts_and_stars_within_one() {\n        assert!(matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billing/invoice.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billing/tax/vat.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/**/mod.rs\", \"src/a/b/mod.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"src/*.rs\", \"src/main.rs\"));\n        assert!(matches(\"docs/billing.md\", \"./docs/billing.md\"));\n        assert!(!matches(\"src/*.rs\", \"src/a/main.rs\"), \"* stays in one part\");\n        assert!(!matches(\"src/billing/**\", \"src/billingx/a.rs\"));\n        assert!(!matches(\"docs/billing.md\", \"docs/billing.mdx\"));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn an_entry_reads_its_paths_and_is_given_once_where_it_is_relevant() {\n        let file = \"---\\npaths: src/billing/**, \\\"docs/billing.md\\\"\\n---\\nInvoices round half to even.\\n\";\n        let e = parse(\"rounding.md\", file);\n        assert_eq!(e.name, \"rounding\");\n        assert_eq!(e.paths, [\"src/billing/**\", \"docs/billing.md\"]);\n        assert_eq!(e.text, \"Invoices round half to even.\");\n        let all = [e];\n        let hit = relevant(&all, \"/work/repo/src/billing/a.rs\", &[]);\n        assert_eq!(hit.len(), 1);\n        assert!(relevant(&all, \"/work/repo/src/main.rs\", &[]).is_empty());\n        assert!(relevant(&all, \"src/billing/a.rs\", &[\"rounding\".into()]).is_empty());\n        assert!(told(&hit).contains(\"<corpus name=\\\"rounding\\\">\"));\n        assert!(parse(\"loose.md\", \"No front matter.\").paths.is_empty());\n    }\n}\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c6b70c94-9939-4eb0-b879-945cf25134b6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgyrNsSiDmzM3hvwY4kjc","type":"assistant","uuid":"353aa0fe-9eec-4c9b-9e35-847f79cbf96f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:50:58.206Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
